    "body": "EICMA 2026 • Triumph TF-E Bikes Get Even More Enduro With Updates for the 2027 Model Year\nBentley's Torcal EV Pushes New Orders Into 2028 Before Production Begins\n56 photos\nPhoto: Bentley\nLove it or hate it, the Torcal has a problem that Bentley is glad for. According to chief executive officer Frank-Steffen Walliser, customers putting an order on the British automaker's first electric vehicle today have to wait until 2028 for delivery. Speaking to Automotive News, the big kahuna hasn't disclosed how many units are in the offing for 2027.\nAt the end of the day, the entire first-year allocation has been spoken for, and that's really good news for the model that many among us criticized for being a Porsche Cayenne Electric with a nicer cabin and more in-your-face styling. In a similar fashion to the Ferrari Luce, the Torcal simply does not care about the rational naysayers and the bona fide haters.\nThe Volkswagen Group-controlled manufacturer intends to start production in the first half of 2027, with Crewe serving as the stomping ground of the Torcal. Before criticizing the company for taking a little too much from public debut to the start of series production, bear in mind this is the company's first electric vehicle and the first EV to be assembled in Crewe.\nSelling out for 2027 also indicates that Bentley was right when it decided that there is enough room for a battery-electric model in this very expensive corner of the market, alongside a plethora of internal combustion models. The Torcal is joined by the Continental GT twins, Flying Spur, and the Bentayga in the automaker's core model lineup, with all of them being assembled in Crewe rather than at Volkswagen Group sites across Europe.\nIt's also worth noting that Bentley was right to position the Torcal below the Bentayga price-wise. A little over $220,000 gets you the most basic of specifications in the United States of America for model year 2028, whereas the base version of the Bentayga is nearly $10,000 pricier.\nFor anyone expecting an affordable entry into Bentley ownership, neither product can be considered entry-level despite their Cayenne Electric and Cayenne underpinnings.\nPhoto: Bentley Walliser told Automotive News that Bentley 's electric vehicle has attracted plenty of youngsters and customers who are completely new to the brand, and this matters a lot in the long run. The early preference for the high-output Torcal S is another interesting detail shared by Walliser.\nInstead of the standard 810 horsepower and a ridiculous 852 pound-feet (1,155 Newton-meters) of twist, S buyers get to enjoy 876 horsepower and 996 pound-feet (1,350 Newton-meters) when launch control is used. The S also happens to be quicker and faster. Both rely on a 113.2-kWh battery that delivers a maximum driving range of 373 miles (600 kilometers), and both support 400-kW charging.\nThat means 16 minutes are required in optimal conditions to get the high-voltage battery from 10 to 80 percent. Capable of sprinting to 60 miles per hour (97 kilometers per hour) in 2.8 seconds, the S version tops 162 miles per hour (260 kilometers per hour) despite being listed with direct drive instead of a two-speed tranny for the rear-mounted drive unit.\nWalliser further shared that Torcal and Torcal S customers are willing to spend well beyond sticker. Speaking to Automotive News, he acknowledged that some configurations exceed 300,000 pounds sterling, which is extremely close to 400,000 dollars at current exchange rates.\nVia // Automotive News\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more stories from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\n2028 Bentley Torcal 2027 Bentley Torcal bentley torcal Bentley production\nAbout the author: Mircea Panait\nAfter a 1:43 scale model of a Ferrari 250 GTO sparked Mircea's interest for cars when he was a kid, an early internship at Top Gear sealed his career path. He's most interested in muscle cars and American trucks, but he takes a passing interest in quirky kei cars as well. Full profile\nUP NEXT BMW's M4 Convertible Getting a Battery-Electric Neue Klasse Makeover, New Model Spied in a Premiere",
